## 2. Observation Count

The controlled three-lane matrix produces exactly **450 lane-level observations:**

```
6 task families
× 5 providers
× 5 occurrence points (1, 2, 3, 5, 10)
× 3 lanes (A, B, C)
= 450 lane-level controlled observations
```

Lane C alone produces **150 Compute Governor observations.**

The mutation layer, recovery tests, cross-provider reuse tests, and natural no-harness sessions expand the total evidence package beyond **500 observations.**

All references to observation count in this document use these definitions. "300 controlled observations" does not appear; "450 lane-level" is the correct term.

