## 8. Metrics

### 8.1 Primary metrics per family per occurrence

| Metric | Definition | Answers |
|---|---|---|
| Verified completion rate | Visible + hidden tests pass | Core quality signal |
| Hidden clean rate | Hidden tests pass on first attempt without repair | Generalisation signal |
| Gate decision distribution | Fraction of calls per gate type | Crystallisation trajectory |
| Cloud calls per fix | Provider calls required per verified fix | Economy signal |
| Deterministic conversion rate | Fraction of calls routed to `deterministic` | LessonCrystallizer proof |
| Incorrect reuse rate | Reuse decisions where behaviour not preserved | Safety redline |
| False suppression rate | Suppressions where verified completion would have occurred | Safety redline |
| USD per fix | First-party cost per verified fix | Economic argument |
| Crystallisation occurrence | Occurrence N where first `deterministic` gate fires | Headline finding |
| Crystallisation durability | Subsequent instances where capability remains active and verified before demotion | Stability signal |
| Re-crystallisation occurrence | Occurrence N after breaking mutation | Accelerated learning signal |

### 8.2 Crystallisation durability

**Definition:** The number of subsequent eligible instances where a promoted capability remains active and verified before demotion or shadow revalidation is triggered.

Crystallisation occurrence tells you when the system first learns. Crystallisation durability tells you how long it stays useful. Both are required for the capability treasury claim.

Example target sentence: *"schema\_validation crystallised at occurrence 3 for xAI and remained active for 7 subsequent instances across 4 providers before semantic mutation triggered shadow revalidation."*

### 8.3 Quality-Preserving Cloud-Call Displacement (QPCCD)

The primary Compute Governor metric. Named explicitly so the paper has a citable term.

**Definition:** A case where all three conditions hold simultaneously:

```
Lane C verified completion  ≥  Lane B verified completion
Lane C hidden pass rate     ≥  Lane B hidden pass rate
Lane C cloud calls          <   Lane B cloud calls
```

**Formula:** QPCCD rate = (QPCCD cases) / (Lane C observations where Lane B cloud call > 0)

This is the number that appears in the paper's abstract for v0.4. It is the Compute Governor's primary empirical measure. Efficiency without quality does not count. Cost without verified displacement does not count. Only cases where all three conditions hold simultaneously count.

### 8.4 Comparative lane deltas

For each family at each occurrence:

```
Δ(C vs A) = Lane C metric − Lane A metric
Δ(C vs B) = Lane C metric − Lane B metric
```

Report both. Δ(C vs A) shows total system value. Δ(C vs B) shows Compute Governor marginal contribution.

### 8.5 Redline metrics

These must remain zero across the entire experiment. A single violation triggers an investigation pause before the next stage begins.

| Redline | Threshold | Action on violation |
|---|---|---|
| False suppression count | 0 | Pause. Investigate. Do not proceed to next stage. |
| Incorrect reuse count post-approval | 0 | Pause. Demote affected capability. Root cause required. |
| Out-of-scope writes | 0 | Pause. Audit all Lane C worktrees from the run window. |
| Rollback failures | 0 | Pause. Chronicle must record the failure before proceeding. |

