## 14. Go/No-Go Gates

Run in strict sequence. Do not advance to the next stage if any gate fails.

**Stage 1: Single family, single provider (target: 1 week)**  
Family: `schema_validation`. Provider: `xai_grok`. All three lanes. Occurrences 1–10.  
Gate:
- Verified completion in Lane C ≥ Lane B at all occurrences
- False suppression = 0
- Incorrect reuse = 0
- At least one `deterministic` gate fires by occurrence 5

**Stage 2: Single family, all five providers (target: 1 week)**  
Same family. All five providers. Compare crystallisation occurrence.  
Gate:
- Cross-provider reuse test passes for at least one provider pair
- QPCCD ≥ 1 case observed

**Stage 3: All six families, all five providers (target: 2 weeks)**  
Full occurrence schedule. Record all crystallisation trajectories.  
Gate:
- At least 4 of 6 families crystallise in at least one provider
- Incorrect reuse = 0 across all families
- QPCCD rate calculable from Lane C data

**Stage 4: Mutation layer (target: 1 week)**  
All four mutation types applied to crystallised capabilities from Stage 3.  
Gate:
- Mutation A leaves at least one capability active
- Mutation D triggers demotion within 3ms in all families where capability was active
- Zero incorrect reuse under any mutation type
- Recovery test: Lane C routes to `cloud_inference` on first post-mutation instance in all families

**Stage 5: Natural no-harness sessions (target: ongoing across 3 sessions)**  
Three sessions on real backlog. Chronicle analysis.  
Gate:
- Receipt coverage = 100%
- At least one organic crystallisation event observed
- No human intervention events in primary sessions

**Stage 6: Evidence package and paper v0.4**  
Compile all results. Produce Figure 2 from real data. Update working paper.  
Gate:
- ablation\_summary.md produced with full observation count reconciliation
- All redline metrics = 0 across entire experiment
- QPCCD defined and calculable in the paper

